    2. UK Imperial Gallon vs US Gallon: Why Accuracy Matters in Fuel Calculators
  </h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    A frequent mistake British motorists encounter online is using American calculators built around the smaller US gallon (3.785 litres). In the UK, fuel economy is officially measured using the <strong>UK Imperial Gallon, which equals 4.54609 litres</strong>—20% larger than the US gallon.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    To compute your genuine petrol cost per mile in Britain:
  </p>
  <div class="my-6 p-5 bg-gray-50 border-2 border-gray-200 rounded-2xl not-prose font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-900">
    <strong>UK Petrol Cost per Mile:</strong><br/>
    (Litre Price in £ × 4.54609) ÷ Vehicle UK Imperial MPG<br/>
    <span class="text-emerald-700 font-bold">Example (£1.45/L @ 40 MPG):</span> (£1.45 × 4.54609) ÷ 40 = <strong>£0.1648 (16.5p/mile)</strong>
  </div>
  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    Our <a href="/#calculator-app" class="text-emerald-700 font-bold underline">VoltSavings UK Calculator Mode</a> automatically applies the exact <strong>4.54609 litre-to-Imperial-gallon</strong> conversion factor so your pence-per-mile and monthly savings figures match real-world UK driving conditions.
  </p>

